{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CexG2HfF6ER7CVUqiihkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EFymjBekyTxnGVW82AHwuk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Add test methods to ShipmentControllerTest.kt","prompt":"Add four new test methods to the ShipmentControllerTest.kt file at /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-1a8cbbfb-17f7-4379-9a7e-1468fe93997a/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt\n\nInsert these test methods BEFORE the closing brace of the class (line 84).\n\nTest 1: Confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED`() {\n    mockMvc.perform(createShipment(\"S-confirm-1\"))\n        .andExpect(status().isCreated)\n\n    // Confirm the shipment\n    mockMvc.perform(post(\"/shipments/S-confirm-1/confirm\")\n        .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON))\n        .andExpect(status().isOk)\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.shipmentId\").value(\"S-confirm-1\"))\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.status\").value(\"CONFIRMED\"))\n\n    // Verify persistence by fetching it again\n    mockMvc.perform(get(\"/shipments/S-confirm-1\"))\n        .andExpect(status().isOk)\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.status\").value(\"CONFIRMED\"))\n}\n```\n\nTest 2: Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment (idempotency)\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing`() {\n    mockMvc.perform(createShipment(\"S-confirm-2\"))\n        .andExpect(status().isCreated)\n\n    // First confirm\n    mockMvc.perform(post(\"/shipments/S-confirm-2/confirm\")\n        .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON))\n        .andExpect(status().isOk)\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.status\").value(\"CONFIRMED\"))\n\n    // Second confirm (idempotent)\n    mockMvc.perform(post(\"/shipments/S-confirm-2/confirm\")\n        .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON))\n        .andExpect(status().isOk)\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.status\").value(\"CONFIRMED\"))\n}\n```\n\nTest 3: Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `confirming a CANCELLED shipment is rejected with 409`() {\n    // Create a shipment\n    mockMvc.perform(createShipment(\"S-confirm-3\"))\n        .andExpect(status().isCreated)\n\n    // Manually set it to CANCELLED in the repository (simulating internal state)\n    val cancelledShipment = Shipment(\n        shipmentId = \"S-confirm-3\",\n        orderId = \"O-1\",\n        carrier = \"DHL\",\n        status = ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED,\n    )\n    repository.save(cancelledShipment)\n\n    // Attempt to confirm the cancelled shipment\n    mockMvc.perform(post(\"/shipments/S-confirm-3/confirm\")\n        .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON))\n        .andExpect(status().isConflict)\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.error.code\").value(\"SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED\"))\n}\n```\n\nTest 4: Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404`() {\n    mockMvc.perform(post(\"/shipments/S-nonexistent/confirm\")\n        .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON))\n        .andExpect(status().isNotFound)\n        .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.error.code\").value(\"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\"))\n}\n```\n\nWrite the complete updated file with all four test methods added before the closing brace. Use the same style, imports, and patterns as the existing tests in the file.","run_in_background":false},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2395,"cache_read_input_tokens":20677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2395,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"conte